<section class="page-intro">
  <h1 id="quality-title">Quality: Lily Core</h1>
  <p class="page-intro-tagline">Lily Core is the set of components Lily is prepared to call proven. A component enters Core only when its evidence is in the repository. <strong>Today Core has no members.</strong> No candidate meets the criteria yet: the screen-reader matrix has no recorded results, so criterion (c) fails for every candidate.</p>
</section>

<section class="prose">
  <h2>What Core means</h2>
  <p>Core is drawn from the 40 interactive components an external audit would look at first: the form family, the five helper pickers, dialogs, tabs, menus, accordion, navigation, pagination, tables and the skip link. These are the candidates. A candidate becomes a member only when all three criteria below hold, and only Core members may be called proven.</p>
  <h2>The criteria</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Keyboard and ARIA-state tests in all eight libraries</strong> (Svelte, React, Vue, Angular, HTML, Web Components, Nunjucks, Blazor). A test file counts when it sends a key event and asserts an <code>aria-*</code> attribute; the key event is waived for a component whose contract names no keys.</li>
    <li><strong>End-to-end tests in Chromium, Firefox and WebKit.</strong></li>
    <li><strong>A filled screen-reader row</strong> with a pass or minor result for each of: NVDA + Firefox, NVDA + Chrome, JAWS + Chrome, VoiceOver + Safari (macOS), VoiceOver (iOS), TalkBack + Chrome (Android).</li>
  </ol>
  <h2>Where the candidates stand</h2>
  <p>Keyboard and ARIA-state tests in all eight libraries: 3 of 40. End-to-end in all three browsers: 38 of 40. Screen-reader row filled: 0 of 40. All three: 0.</p>
  <p>Why none has met them: the <a href="https://github.com/LilyDesignSystem/lily-design-system/blob/main/docs/screen-reader-matrix.md">screen-reader matrix</a> has 0 of 120 cells filled, because no one has yet run the components with a screen reader and recorded the result, and this project does not record results it has not observed. 17 candidates have no row in the matrix yet. The end-to-end suites run in Chromium, Firefox, WebKit.</p>
</section>

